hi

you can use a function in dplyr called filter_ it accepts strings as arguments (as do all functions with suffix of “_“ in dplyr)
library(dplyr)
set.seed(8)
df=data.frame(x=rnorm(10),y=runif(10))
x y
-0.08459 0.2237
0.8404 0.4079
-0.4635 0.6149
-0.5508 0.215
0.736 0.6633
-0.1079 0.9775
-0.1703 0.09775
-1.088 0.6119
-3.011 0.5276
-0.5932 0.8174
df%>%filter_("x< -3")
x y
-3.011 0.5276

yoni
​

